!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/link/invalid/a-member-through-its-operands-heads-applied-parent-that-does-not-pin-the-discriminator-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/link-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.8, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.10"
  description: """
    `abstract` on a parametric record is each application's `extension`, so `tb`, declaring `box<text>`, is an
    abstract base dispatching on `kind`. `boxed` absorbs `wrap<text>`, whose head's written parent is `box<text>`
    there, so `boxed` IS-A `tb`, and joining a family through those parents brings its obligation: the member pins
    the family's discriminators. `boxed` leaves `kind` unpinned, as the declared `wrap<text>` would.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
